Arbalet is an Opensource & OpenHardware LED Table, a flat surface filled with several hundreds of coloured square lights. It is designed for Teaching of programming, Geeks, and Pleasure. With its limited number of pixels, Arbalet brings our old 80 arcad games back into fashion through a modern, classy, and hackable device.
This timelapse shows how to build a LED table using laser cutting and DIY material in a fablab. 
To keep in touch: twitter.com/arbalet_project
Wanna build your own? Follow the guide: arbalet-project.org
